# =============================================================================
# Frontend — Environment Variables
# =============================================================================
# Copy to .env.local for development, and set the same values on the host for
# deploys (docs/deployment.md). Never commit .env.local.
#
# Nothing here is required to boot: every NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_* falls back to the
# default shown, which is what the upstream site uses. Setting none of them
# gives you upstream's branding; setting them makes the site yours without
# touching a line of code. Source of truth: src/lib/constants.ts
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at BUILD time — restart `npm run dev` after editing,
# and redeploy (not just restart) after changing them on a host.
# =============================================================================

# --- Identity ---
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_NAME=d3jusdevspace
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_TAGLINE=AI engineer, builder, thinker
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_DESCRIPTION=Personal knowledge hub, blog, and AI Agent collaboration blogging platform
# Used for absolute URLs — sitemap.xml, robots.txt, OpenGraph. Set this to the
# real domain before launch or search engines get localhost.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# --- Hero and byline ---
# AUTHOR is the short display name in the hero pill and sidebar; ROLE sits
# under it in uppercase mono, so keep it short. INTRO is plain prose, no markup.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_AUTHOR=d3ju
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_ROLE=AI/ML Engineer
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_INTRO=I'm just another human finding my voice in a noisy world. Here, I'm a Full-Stack AI/ML Engineer, and I document my projects, lessons, ideas, thoughts, and basically, just ME. Hope you find something for you!

# --- Footer ---
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_MOTTO=BUILT FOR THE AGENTIC AGE

# --- Links --- leave LINKEDIN blank to hide that link rather than dead-end it
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_REPO=https://github.com/DejusDevspace/my-blog
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_GITHUB=https://github.com/DejusDevspace
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_TWITTER=https://x.com/adejo_deju
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_LINKEDIN=https://linkedin.com/in/deju-adejo

# --- Look ---
# Favicon, served from public/. Not the app/icon.* file convention: that
# resolves from the filesystem at build time and can't be overridden per fork.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_ICON=/favicon.ico
# Palette — one file in src/styles/themes/, applied as data-skin on <html>.
# Independent of light/dark, which works within whichever skin is active.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_SKIN=cyber-luxury
# Which mode a first-time visitor gets: system | light | dark. The navbar
# toggle overrides this and is remembered, so pinning one never hides the other.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_THEME=system

# =============================================================================
# Server-side only — never sent to the browser, no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix.
# =============================================================================

# Signs the JWT the FastAPI backend validates. Must match NEXTAUTH_SECRET in
# backend/.env exactly, or every admin request returns 401.
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
NEXTAUTH_SECRET=

# The deployed URL in production; http://localhost:3000 in development.
NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Admin sign-in. Checked directly by src/lib/auth.ts, not stored anywhere.
# ADMIN_EMAIL must match the backend's ADMIN_EMAIL — it's the claim the
# backend looks up to find the owner row.
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@d3jusdevspace.com
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Where /api/proxy/* forwards to. Defaults to localhost:8000, so it is only
# needed when the backend runs elsewhere (i.e. always, once deployed).
# BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8000

# Authenticates Vercel Cron calls to /api/cron/agent. Unset = that route
# refuses every request, including Vercel's — it is a public URL, so it fails
# closed rather than open. Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
CRON_SECRET=
